35,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, the numbers are in! It turns out the ""complaints"" are mostly coming from one specific house, and our frontages are definitely not equal. Some of us have way more room to breathe than others. Interesting, right?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"That is a significant detail, May. It suggests the issue might be more about specific perspectives than a general failure. I've found that some ""solutions"" can actually worsen the environment, especially during the summer months.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, I found some big numbers! Last year's shelters cost a lot, but the ward gives some money back. Also, we're spending thousands every year just on nets and smells because of the open bags!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It sounds like we have a lot to think about. I noticed that most complaints come from one household, and at the meeting, people were hesitant to police each other. I'm worried about the tension this creates between us.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is enlightening to hear your findings. I have learned that the truck arrives quite early, and the bureaucracy for a permanent structure is quite demanding. We must be careful not to create a system that is too rigid.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, spending thousands on nets is a bit much, isn't it? And @Midori, since the complaints are so one-sided, it's clear the current setup is a burden for one person. We can't just ignore that imbalance.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, while addressing the imbalance is necessary, we must be cautious. I've seen that enclosed structures can trap odors and become worse in August. A ""fair"" solution that creates a permanent smell is not a solution at all.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, that's a good point! But if we keep spending money on deodorants and nets every year, that's also a problem. Maybe there's a way to keep it fresh without spending too much?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, you're right that the burden is uneven. But if we focus only on the space, we might miss the feelings involved. I want us to find a way to resolve this without anyone feeling singled out or resentful.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"True harmony is found when we balance the physical needs with the human spirit. If the rules are too strict and the hours too early, we risk exhausting the very people we wish to support. Let us be mindful of the time.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,May,,"@Servas, I agree we shouldn't be exhausted, but we can't be lazy about fairness either. If one person has been stuck with the bins at their gate for years, ""harmony"" means actually moving them or sharing the load.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@May, moving the bins is a logical step, but we must consider the daily reality. If we simply shift the location, we might just move the annoyance to another neighbor. We need a system that manages the environment, not just the position.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, @May, I'm thinking about the money again. If we build something fancy to stop the smells, it might cost a lot! We need to make sure everyone can afford the bill, no matter their budget.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, I agree. Financial stress can lead to more arguments. I just hope we don't let the cost or the location become a reason for us to stop talking to each other. Let's be gentle with one another.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,Money and space are but the surface of the water. The true current is the time and energy we give. Let us ensure our plan does not quietly drain the spirit of a few.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,May,,"Exactly, @Servas! That's my point. ""Sharing the load"" shouldn't just be a phrase; it needs to be a reality. If we just sign a paper without changing the physical burden, we're not being fair, we're just being polite.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"Politeness without a practical foundation is fragile, May. We must ensure the chosen arrangement is sustainable for the person living beside it every single day, especially in the heat, or the complaints will simply shift.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! Let's find a way to stop those smells and the waste of money on nets, but without making it too expensive for anyone. I'm sure we can find a balance that makes everyone happy!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I hope we can all agree that our relationship as neighbors is the most valuable thing here. Let's choose an option that solves the practical problems while bringing us closer together, rather than creating new divisions.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Indeed. Let us remember that the most enduring structures are not made of wood or stone, but of mutual respect. I look forward to seeing the options and choosing a path that honors everyone's time and peace.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
